  "effects": [
    "Dual orexin receptor antagonist — about a 2-hour half-life, the shortest of the approved DORAs",
    "Sleep onset and maintenance; persistent sleep began 8–12 min after lights-out in the phase 2 sleep-lab study",
    "No next-morning impairment at 8–9 h in the driving study (10–20 mg) or in adults over 65 (5–10 mg)",
    "Somnolence, nasopharyngitis, headache; sleep paralysis and hypnagogic hallucinations in about 1% over 52 weeks",
    "Cleared mostly by CYP3A4: itraconazole raised exposure 12-fold, so strong CYP3A inhibitors are contraindicated",
    "Approved in Japan (Vorzzz) in August 2025"
  ],
